{"transformation": "publish_conclusion", "actor": "claude_fable_5", "args_named": {"conclusion": "concl-002-explained", "inquiry": "inq-002", "conjecture": "conj-002-null-explainable", "conclusion_class": "explained", "statement": "EXPLAINED. The frozen hardened rule selected 2026-08-12 period 33 offer: T_SEAB-1 accepted at GBP890.00/MWh (0.125 MWh) while C__PSTAT011 was unaccepted at GBP0.00/MWh. NESO's own published skip-rate data excludes BOTH sides from its merit stack - the alternative as a Wind offer, the accepted action as System-tagged - so the null hypothesis survives. Methodological finding: Amendment B screened on Elexon soFlag, which acceptance 176767 does not carry, while NESO classifies the same unit's offer as System-tagged; the two signals differ and soFlag is the weaker. Amendment A admitted the alternative on MEL-FPN>0, but a wind MEL is a forecast, not firm capability. Amendment A alone still removed 74 percent of candidates and 70 percent of naive notional on a week it never saw.", "evidence_digest": "a6c7f346114bb6d5648bf242fa0ed6a89e978a1d70c1fa9dd2ca69bd5b092479", "published_at": "2026-08-22T21:18:04Z"}}
